-# NFSU2 Driving Tools: experimental v0.30.0
+# NFSU2 Driving Tools: experimental v0.31.0
 
 Unpacked Chrome / Edge / Brave extension for https://nfsu2.xyz/. See `CHANGELOG.md` for this release's changes and verification limits.
 
-## v0.30.0: Compact driving information HUD
+## v0.31.0: Keep owned Drag AI through settings refreshes
+
+A reproduced publication race could let the game's manual-Drag selector run while the extension refreshed the same active settings. The new guard retains an **already-owned, currently permitted native Drag AI lease** through that brief write. It does not acquire new control, force a real manual request back to AI, or change steering, shifting, NOS or damage.
+
+A separate fix ensures a pause/end/OFF command is acknowledged by the native game before a quick restart can overwrite it. This also covers consecutive matches that reuse the same player, car and race objects. It does not clear the game's failed-control latch while AI remains continuously requested.
+
+**F7/manual takeover, F9/OFF, native finish/totaled states, permission withdrawal, identity changes and the 180-native-frame watchdog remain effective.** Do not use this as a no-crash, no-damage or guaranteed-win feature. Online use still requires the existing explicit Allow network tools opt-in.
+
+The fresh user log shows a request for manual Drag before the observed handback, matching the reproduced ordering. It does not record the rejecting guard, so this is not proof of that run's exact cause. The log came from v0.28. Live handoff prevention remains unverified.
+
+Only the Drag input guard changes in the two supported modern native profiles. The HUD, tuner/static-ride fix, NOS clock correction, working Street X behavior, Drift isolation, saved profiles, collision/corner settings and engine-blowout protection remain combined. No unrelated lane candidate or unverified grip/downforce activation is included.
+
+**Verification:** the final combined suite passes 1,873 tests with no failures/skips/cancellations. Exact-native tests exercise retained ownership, real manual requests, OFF acknowledgement and watchdog release; the menu shortcut has five focused tests, including closed-shadow paste behavior. Browser appearance and live race efficacy remain unverified.
+
+**Shift+Insert** now toggles the full tools menu, alongside F8. It does not intercept Paste while typing in text/editable controls. Holding the shortcut does not repeatedly toggle it. Closing follows the same existing menu behavior, including cancelling a running tuner operation.
+
+Reload after enabling only v0.31 and verify the **0.31.0** badge. Keep your chosen settings; start the race yourself. If the unwanted handback persists, export a short new crash log immediately after it occurs.
+
+## Retained v0.30.0: Compact driving information HUD
 
 A small, click-through **Info HUD** appears below the upper-right launcher while the tools menu is closed. **F6** toggles it, or open **F8 → Info HUD**. It starts on and remembers only its display choice in this tab, separately from driving-tool profiles. Opening the menu hides the card until you close it. F7 returns control and F9 still stops driving assists; the HUD itself never enables them.
 
